{"id": "tea:nadabindu-upanisad:1", "source": "src:nadabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1"}, "paraphrase": "Oṃ is a bird: a is its right wing, u its left, m its tail, and the half-measure its head.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["sound-language"], "concepts": ["cpt:omkara-matras"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:nadabindu-upanisad:21-29", "source": "src:nadabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "21-29"}, "paraphrase": "For the knower, prārabdha karma is not destroyed by knowledge alone but its hold is like the objects of a dream on one who has woken; as the snake seen in a rope, the body and world are superimposed; knowledge destroys accumulated and future karma.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:prarabdha-of-the-knower"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:nadabindu-upanisad:31", "source": "src:nadabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "31"}, "paraphrase": "Seated in siddhāsana, holding the vaiṣṇavī mudrā, the yogin should always listen to the inner sound in the right ear.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice", "sound-language"], "practices": ["prc:nadanusandhana", "prc:vaisnavi-mudra"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:nadabindu-upanisad:33-35", "source": "src:nadabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "33-35"}, "paraphrase": "At first the sounds are loud — like the ocean, clouds, kettledrum and waterfall; in the middle, like the mardala drum, bell and horn; at the end, like tinkling bells, flute, vīṇā and bee.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["sound-language", "powers-experiences"], "concepts": ["cpt:nada"], "paths": ["pth:nadabindu-nada-stages"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:nadabindu-upanisad:38-39", "source": "src:nadabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "38-39"}, "paraphrase": "Hearing the subtler sound within the loud, the mind fixed on it does not wander; it becomes one with nāda like milk mixed with water and quickly dissolves in the space of consciousness.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind"], "concepts": ["cpt:nada", "cpt:unmani"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:nadabindu-upanisad:42-46", "source": "src:nadabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "42-46"}, "paraphrase": "As the bee drinking honey does not care for fragrance, the mind absorbed in nāda does not crave objects; nāda is the charm that stills the snake of the mind, the goad for the elephant of mind, the net for the deer of mind, the shore for the ocean of mind.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "practice"], "concepts": ["cpt:nada"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:nadabindu-upanisad:47-48", "source": "src:nadabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "47-48"}, "paraphrase": "The sound lasts only while there is space; the soundless is the supreme Brahman, the supreme Self. As long as there is sound there is mind; the end of sound is the state beyond mind (manonmanī).", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate", "sound-language"], "concepts": ["cpt:nada", "cpt:unmani"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:nadabindu-upanisad:52-56", "source": "src:nadabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "52-56"}, "paraphrase": "The yogin absorbed in nāda lies like a dead man, his body like a log, unaware of heat and cold, pleasure and pain, honour and dishonour; his gaze, breath and mind are steady without support — he is liberated.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["powers-experiences", "karma-liberation"], "concepts": ["cpt:unmani"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:nadabindu-upanisad:9-16", "source": "src:nadabindu-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "9-16"}, "paraphrase": "The twelve measures (ghoṣiṇī, vidyunmātrā, pataṅginī, vāyuveginī, nāmadheyā, aindrī, vaiṣṇavī, śāṅkarī, mahatī, dhṛti, nārī, brāhmī) each give a destiny to one who dies in it — from a universal king, yakṣa, vidyādhara and gandharva, to the worlds of Soma, Indra, Viṣṇu and Rudra, the Mahar, Jana and Tapas worlds, and in the last, the eternal Brahman.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["sound-language", "death-dying"], "concepts": ["cpt:omkara-matras", "cpt:destiny-by-matra-at-death"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
